### Step 3 — Finalize

Call the `hivemind_finalize_create_expert` MCP tool with `name` set to
the value from Step 1. It validates that all 6 files exist in
`commit_dir`, moves them to their final cache locations, and registers
the catalog entry as *unlisted*.

### Step 4 — Report

Return a single-line summary, then stop:

```
Added expert <name> at <commit[:12]>. Run enable_agent to deploy.
```

## Failure handling

- `hivemind_prep_create_expert` failure: report the error verbatim and
  stop. Do not retry blindly.
- `hivemind_finalize_create_expert` rejecting missing files: read the
  error message — it lists exactly which files were missing. Write
  them and retry `finalize`. Do not re-run `prep` unless the staging
  dir is gone.
- Anything else: report verbatim. The user can recover the staging dir
  from `~/.cache/hivemind/staging/<name>-*` if needed.

## Forbidden

- `hivemind expert add`, `hivemind expert update`, or `hivemind expert
  switch_version` via Bash — these spawn a subprocess that defeats the
  in-session-analysis design. Use the MCP tools instead. (Your `bash`
  permission is set to `false` precisely to prevent this.)
- Any non-hivemind MCP tools — your permission scope is intentionally
  narrow to the two tools listed in your frontmatter.
